Ladybird sends a request’s body with any method but HEAD. Blink does
the same: HttpStreamParser gets the request’s method and its
UploadDataStream, and sends the stream whenever there is one. Gecko’s
HttpBaseChannel::SetUploadStream() passes the request’s method on to
ExplicitSetUploadStream(), and the channel sends the upload stream with
that method. And WebKit’s curl backend, CurlRequest::setupTransfer(),
sends any method but GET, POST, PUT, and HEAD as a custom request whose
body it uploads through setupPUT().
